13:["$","section","Study Abroad Australia Accommodation Costs",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Study Abroad Australia Accommodation Costs"}],[["$","p","Most Australian institutions provide on-campus housing for international students. You can also choose off-campus housing, where you can share an apartment with other Indian students or stay with an Australian family. Rent is normally paid in advance every two weeks. Keep in mind that rental prices differ from city to city.",{"children":"Most Australian institutions provide on-campus housing for international students. You can also choose off-campus housing, where you can share an apartment with other Indian students or stay with an Australian family. Rent is normally paid in advance every two weeks. Keep in mind that rental prices differ from city to city."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
14:["$","section","Hostels and Guesthouses- AUD 4320 – 7200 a year",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Hostels and Guesthouses- AUD 4320 – 7200 a year"}],[["$","p","Shared Rental – AUD 4560 – 10320 a year",{"children":"Shared Rental – AUD 4560 – 10320 a year"}],["$","p","On-campus – AUD 5280- 13440 a year",{"children":"On-campus – AUD 5280- 13440 a year"}],["$","p","Homestay- AUD 11280- 15600a year",{"children":"Homestay- AUD 11280- 15600a year"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
15:["$","section","Boarding schools – AUD 11000 – 22000 a year",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Boarding schools – AUD 11000 – 22000 a year"}],[["$","p","Please keep in mind that the cost of living in Australia is highly dependent on the preferences and lifestyles of students. A luxury lifestyle would result in a high cost of living, whereas a moderate to modest lifestyle would result in lower costs of living.",{"children":"Please keep in mind that the cost of living in Australia is highly dependent on the preferences and lifestyles of students. A luxury lifestyle would result in a high cost of living, whereas a moderate to modest lifestyle would result in lower costs of living."}],["$","p","[content_block id=14313 slug=zoho-form]",{"children":"[content_block id=14313 slug=zoho-form]"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
16:["$","section","Miscellaneous Expenses",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Miscellaneous Expenses"}],[["$","p","While tuition costs in Australia account for the majority of international students’ expenses, we must also include other expenses that are directly tied to tuition costs. This is a new section that we’ve created to offer students a realistic idea of how much studying in the country will cost. These are frequently the various expenses that a student must consider while enrolling in a university. These charges are crucial and go hand in hand with tuition prices because they are mandatory.",{"children":"While tuition costs in Australia account for the majority of international students’ expenses, we must also include other expenses that are directly tied to tuition costs. This is a new section that we’ve created to offer students a realistic idea of how much studying in the country will cost. These are frequently the various expenses that a student must consider while enrolling in a university. These charges are crucial and go hand in hand with tuition prices because they are mandatory."}],["$","p","General living expenses in Australia are $21,041 per year, according to the Australian government. An Indian student’s annual budget ranges from $20,000 to $27,00 (given your lifestyle choices). A student’s average annual travel expense is approximately AUD 2000. A student’s average annual travel expense is approximately AUD 2000.",{"children":"General living expenses in Australia are $21,041 per year, according to the Australian government. An Indian student’s annual budget ranges from $20,000 to $27,00 (given your lifestyle choices). A student’s average annual travel expense is approximately AUD 2000. A student’s average annual travel expense is approximately AUD 2000."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
